Installations:
--------------
git clone https://github.com/riscv/riscv-gnu-toolchain
Go to https://github.com/riscv/riscv-gnu-toolchain and follow the actual installation instructions.
Be aware, that AMD-Vivado has its own RISC-V toolchain, which is not suited for our needs. But it can be in your execution path.
A possible target for our installation might be /opt/riscv.

Simulation:
-----------
Either Vivado or Verilator.

CMAKE:
------
Install cmake.

Single Test Case Simulation with Verilator Wave:
------------------------------------------------
- rm -rf build
- cmake -S . -B build -DSIMULATOR=verilator -DWAVES=ON
- cmake --build build --target sim_instr38ld
... this makes ...
- -S . * gives the source directory (the dot indicates it is here)
- -B build * defines the target directory and generates it, all binaries will be generated here
- -DSIMULATOR=verilator -DWAVES=ON * defines (-D) two variables, SIMULATOR=verilator and WAVES=ON
- --build build * starts the compilation in the directory build
- --target sim_instr38ld * choses one test case
... under the hood ...
- The directory ./build/instr38ld will be generated (make: set(TEST_BUILD_DIR build/instr38ld) - set(TEST_BUILD_DIR ${CMAKE_BINARY_DIR}/${TEST}))
- 

- cp rv64Sim/instr38ld.asm rv64i.asm (copy the test case to rv64i.asm)
- /opt/riscv/bin/riscv64-unknown-linux-gnu-as -march=rv64i_zicsr -mlittle-endian -g -o rv64i.o rv64i.asm -al=rv64i.lst (assemble)
- /opt/riscv/bin/riscv64-unknown-linux-gnu-ld -b elf64-littleriscv -o rv64i rv64i.o (linking)
- /opt/riscv/bin/riscv64-unknown-linux-gnu-objcopy rv64i -O verilog --verilog-data-width 4 rv64i.v (copy from IntelHex to Verilog)
- sed -i 's/ /\n/g' rv64i.v (replaces spaces by CR)
- sed -i 's/\r//g' rv64i.v (delete ^M at the end of lines if it occurs)
- sed -i '1d' rv64i.v (deletes the first line; not needed here)
- cp -rf rv64i.v ../build/instr38ld/rv64i.mem
- get test bench from ./tb
- simulate

